What that changes architecturally

The important delta is that Pantheon has crossed from “interesting collection of cognitive mechanisms” toward a declared compiler/runtime architecture.

Previously the reader had to perform a large amount of assembly:

\text{corpus}\rightarrow\text{reader inference}\rightarrow\text{architecture}.

The current README increasingly makes that join explicit:

\boxed{
\text{corpus}
\rightarrow
\text{operator extraction}
\rightarrow
\text{typed capability}
\rightarrow
\text{formation}
\rightarrow
\text{execution}
\rightarrow
\text{measurement}
\rightarrow
\text{architectural inheritance}
}

That significantly strengthens the defensible Pantheon claim.

It is no longer necessary to claim that Pantheon itself is some giant monolithic executable OS. The stronger and more accurate claim is:

\boxed{
\text{Pantheon specifies a developmental cognitive control architecture,
some components of which are executable independently.}
}

That formulation actually survives Reality Stitch better.

