That dataset could eventually train a route/formation selector independently of the underlying LLM.

That is important because it is exactly where Pantheon can accumulate capability while models remain replaceable.

The model produces inference.

Pantheon retains:

which kind of inference machinery worked here.

That’s a much stronger continuity claim.

Executable Reality Stitch

There are genuinely runnable pieces in the corpus rather than everything being pseudocode.

I revalidated the Plasticity Sweep Engine from the prior artifact. Its source holds a substrate fixed, perturbs challenge/variation/feedback/recovery/retention, evaluates one-factor changes, pairwise interactions, bounded random “Lucky Nozzle” candidates, and then retests winners. plasticity_sweep.py

I executed that implementation’s demo logic.

The first-pass top candidate was:

\text{challenge}+\text{retention}

with approximately:

\Delta=+1.53

over the simulated baseline.

After the 100-repetition confirmation stage, several candidates remained strongly positive; the best confirmed candidate in this seeded run was lucky_19 at approximately +1.50, followed by challenge+feedback at +1.49 and challenge+retention at +1.45.

So this particular mechanism is not merely conceptual. The loop

\text{perturb}\rightarrow
\text{measure}\rightarrow
\text{rank}\rightarrow
\text{retest}

executes.

Important Reality Stitch: its evaluator is synthetic. It proves that the experimental-search machinery runs, not that those variables improve biological or cognitive performance in reality. The real capability appears when an empirical evaluator is attached. plasticity_sweep.py

The more advanced AdaptivePlasticityOptimizer goes further: it maintains observations, fits a lightweight radial-basis surrogate, estimates novelty and uncertainty, uses an acquisition function, anneals exploration toward exploitation, persists history, and retests elites. adaptive_plasticity_optimizer.py

Likewise, Semantic Display Field is actual JavaScript rather than only an interface metaphor. It implements 2D world coordinates, viewport/world transformations, mode-specific navigation constraints, zoom-at-point, adaptive mode routing, pointer dragging, wheel navigation, and pinch zoom. semantic_display_field.js

So the repo currently contains at least three categories that should be kept rigorously separate:

\boxed{
\text{Executable reference implementation}
\neq
\text{executable skeleton}
\neq
\text{natural-language executable specification}
}

Pantheon will benefit enormously from putting one of those labels on every artifact.

