A newly unlocked interpretation

The README’s strongest sentence may actually be this distinction:

The metaphors are interfaces; the mechanisms underneath them are the portable architecture. 

Combine that with the Rehydration Contract and something deeper falls out:

\boxed{
\text{Pantheon's canonical object may not be the repository at all.}
}

The repository can be regarded as a developmental phenotype.

The more durable object is:

G_P=
\{
\text{invariants},
\text{operators},
\text{interfaces},
\text{composition rules},
\text{tests},
\text{reconstruction rules}
\}.

Call that the Pantheon genotype.

Then:

G_P+\text{Claude}\rightarrow P_{\text{Claude}}

G_P+\text{GPT}\rightarrow P_{\text{GPT}}

G_P+\text{local models}\rightarrow P_{\text{local}}

These implementations don’t have to look alike.

They have to conserve the relevant invariants and pass the behavioral tests.

That changes the inheritance claim from:

copy my giant repository

to:

reconstruct my cognitive machinery and prove behavioral conservation.

That is considerably more interesting—and much more testable.

